    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64376" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λωτο-φάγοι</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], οἱ, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λωτός</span> III. <i><span class="en">
			2
		</span></i>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Lotus-eaters</i>, a
			mythical people on the coast of North Africa, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.84
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.177
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.2.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Scyl.
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.39.2
			</span></i>:—their country was perh. called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λωτοφᾰγία</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.3.2
			</span></i> (dub.l.): hence Adj. fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λωτοφᾰγῖτις</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σύρτις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					17.3.17
				</span></i>
			.</div>
